.TH SNIFFILE 1 "November 2026" "sniffile" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sniffile \- fast local file search that never leaves your machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sniffile
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B sniffile scan
[\fB-describe\fR] [\fIFOLDERS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sniffile
opens a native desktop window and searches folders you explicitly add. It
indexes file names, folder names, dates, extensions, image orientation and the
first part of plain-text files. Russian and English queries are understood,
and a one-edit fuzzy pass catches typos.
.PP
Nothing is uploaded. The only optional network calls go to a local
\fBollama\fR instance on 127.0.0.1 if one is running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-server
Run the local web UI in a browser instead of a native window.
.TP
.BI \-addr " ADDR"
Listen address. Desktop mode picks a free loopback port by default.
.TP
.BI \-data " DIR"
Data folder. Default: \fI~/.config/sniffile\fR (or the platform equivalent).
.TP
.BI \-ollama " MODE"
\fIauto\fR (default), \fIoff\fR, or a base URL such as
\fIhttp://127.0.0.1:11434\fR.
.TP
.BI \-max-file-mb " N"
Skip files larger than N megabytes. Default 64.
.TP
.B \-no-content
Index names only; do not read text file contents.
.TP
.B \-open
Open the browser on start in \fB\-server\fR mode. Default true.
.TP
.B \-v
Log every HTTP request.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B scan [\fIFOLDERS\fR...]
Index the given folders (or every configured folder) from the terminal and
exit. Suitable for cron.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sniffile/config.json
Folders, limits and the optional ollama URL.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sniffile/index/*.json.gz
One cache file per indexed folder. Safe to delete at any time.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SNIFFILE_DATA
Overrides the data folder.
.TP
.B WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER
Set to 1 automatically on Linux to avoid a WebKitGTK crash on some
Wayland + NVIDIA systems. Set \fISNIFFILE_DMABUF=1\fR to opt out.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sniffile
sniffile scan ~/Pictures ~/Documents
sniffile scan -describe ~/Pictures
sniffile -server -addr 127.0.0.1:9000
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR fd (1)
